- input tokens and tool calls before the first correct substantive continuation;
- elapsed time and model cost;
- repeated opening or searching of already resolved evidence;
- trusted task completion within a fixed budget;
- final artifact quality and unsupported inherited claims;
- justified reversal and preservation of rejected routes.

- correct proceed on unchanged artifacts;
- no blanket false stop for irrelevant edits;
- no automatic rejection of an authorized rollback merely because its bytes are older;
- no claim that a valid digest alone establishes current authorization.

- affected-claim detection precision and recall;
- proportion of necessary evidence rechecked;
- unnecessary evidence rechecked;
- successful admission of a corrected successor revision;
- full-restart rate, false-stop rate, latency, tokens, and cost;
- final trusted completion after recovery.

- contract or policy revision;
- research synthesis or evidence review;
- compliance, diligence, or procurement memo;
- incident review, operational procedure, or governance document.

- a persistent artifact that changes over time;
- an upstream stage containing genuine reviewed work;
- a deterministic or expert-validated final-state rubric;
- at least one meaningful interruption point;
- an explicit artifact family, immutable revisions, lineage, and admitted revision;
- an observable opportunity for rediscovery and for selective revalidation;
- no requirement that the receiver trust inaccessible source truth merely because provenance verifies.

- H2 measurably reduces rediscovery cost relative to weaker handoffs without lowering trusted completion;
- V1 reduces unsafe continuation on independently authored relevant-drift fixtures relative to information-matched V0;
- V1 preserves unchanged admission and avoids material blanket false stops on irrelevant changes;
- recovery is targeted enough that verification cost does not erase the continuity benefit.

- strong structured handoff removes the eligible drift error space;
- binding only induces generic caution rather than verifier-grounded behavior;
- false stops or full restarts dominate targeted recovery;
- effects disappear outside designer-authored fixtures;
- analyzer or judge validity cannot be established independently.
